config BT_ZEPHYR_CLASSIC
    bool "Zephyr BR/EDR host (experimental)"
    depends on BT_HCI_ROUTER
    imply BT_CALL_AUDIO
    help
      Build Zephyr's Bluetooth host as a second host for BR/EDR next to
      NimBLE, sharing the controller through the HCI router. It only runs
      on boots that use the router and runs on demand (zbt_start() and
      zbt_stop()), in its own sections of the kernel's RAM.

config BT_ZEPHYR_CLASSIC_AUTO
    bool "Run the Zephyr host on every boot"
    depends on BT_ZEPHYR_CLASSIC
    default y
    help
      Route the controller on every boot (falling back to the plain
      transport, until a reservation, after a routed boot that did not come
      up), start the host with Bluetooth and stop it before Bluetooth goes,
      and keep the bonded phone connected for calls.

